{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##|G4|G5|G14|G18'\"' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '85,145p' docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md\ncat data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/result.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:9:## Answer and review scope\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:24:## Goals and current coverage\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:37:## Additional explicit findings\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:39:### G11. Whole-report coverage and narrative formalisation need a procedure\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:41:Requirements: MC01, MC03. Refines G2 and G5.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:60:### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:62:Requirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:79:### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:81:Requirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:98:### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:119:### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:138:### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:156:### G17. Local evidence review needs a state machine and invalidation rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:158:Requirements: MC04, MC27. Refines G2, G5 and G10.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:174:### G18. Reproducibility needs identity and replay definitions, not only fields\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:193:## Completion consequences\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:213:## Evidence and limits of this pass\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:7:## Question, baseline and skeptical audit\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:33:## Findings\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:47:### G1. Reconstruction defines the answer more precisely than the algorithm\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:73:### G2. The normative language and IR contracts remain incomplete\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:98:### G3. Ordinary disclosure uncertainty can leave the promised solver fragment\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:124:### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:145:### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:164:### G6. Forward economic and probability models remain interfaces\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:192:### G7. Standards, banks and insurance are largely deferred requirements\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:218:### G8. Literature breadth exceeds the depth of the follow-up screening\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:246:### G9. Tool selection is a shortlist, without demonstrated adapter contracts\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:265:### G10. Acceptance and completion are not yet determinate\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:289:## Prioritised repair sequence\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:306:## Review evidence and limits\nthis grant.\n\nThe status command uses the same prefix and never starts workers. A stop command\nrequests bounded child termination and preserves partial work. Normal run resumes\nafter a previous stop. --retry-blocked is reserved for deliberately retrying a\nknown external block after changed access or environment; ordinary resume does\nnot repeatedly probe it.\n\n## Evidence and scope\n\nThe accepted financial-report corpus remains frozen and source-complete for its\ndeclared panel. Master outputs go under data/accounting-master; original release\nhashes are not rewritten to conceal changes. Existing Git remains unusable and\nhas not been initialised. Prior editable source bytes are retained before phase\nworkers change them. New source research must preserve provenance and limitations.\n\nPlanning, implementation and read-only review run sequentially, with no nested\nagents. The upfront grant is scoped to this program, its filesystem sandboxes,\nlegitimate public-source research and project-local work. It does not authorise\nprofessional fees, paid data/accounts, deployment, outreach or global packages.\n\nA bounded accepted phase does not close its wider accounting/design gap. The\nrefreshed plan retains residuals and next actions; independent work continues\nwhile external/human acceptance is pending. P00/P01 preflights passed after a\nbaseline import-path repair. Full execution and reviewer verdicts are recorded\nby the runner, not assumed here.\n\nThis checkpoint is the current assessment supplement to the frozen mission\nregister. P02 advances MC01/MC03/MC05/MC16/MC28 through selected source-bound\ndispositions and reconciliations. P03 supplies provisional engineering evidence\nfor MC02/MC04/MC10/MC20/MC23/MC24. All 35 requirements map to catalog phases;\nall G1–G18 remain open and `mission_complete` remains false. Feasible internal\nwork continues before paid professional review; no engagement or fee is authorised.\n# P04 bounded reconstruction result\n\nPASS: 21 P04 tests executed; observations cover 21/21 catalogued obligations; 11 P03 regression tests executed. Full executed outcomes, formulas, cell assignments, witnesses, conflicts, source hashes and proof queries are in conformance.json.\n\nThe current recovery accepts explicit supervisor approval and execution-inventory paths, checks approval structure and plan-hash integrity, and retains the original design and historical inventory separately. Four checker obligations exercise malformed or unapproved inputs, rejection before writes, current manifest selection, unchanged protection exclusions and failure reporting in disposable trees. Their simulated test outcomes concern reporting behavior only; the reconstruction tests supply the numerical evidence below.\n\nDeclared templates construct account and economic-state roll-forwards. Independent Fraction enumeration checks three finite input variants; a selected Northstar receivables bridge replays original events to create observations before reconstruction. P03 integration preserves alpha=1/2, isolates endpoint conditions, retains overlapping views and rejects incompatible joint extrema. Parent coverage remains one continuous cell without genuine choices.\n\nExact debt interest ranges from 5 to 7. The rounded fixture has infimum 199/40, attained, and supremum 1407/200, unattained. Original strict feasibility precedes closure optimisation. Half-even negative ties, posting minor units, integer gaps, source conflicts, unsupported arithmetic, zero budgets and injected Unknown responses are checked. Incomplete search retains domains, predicates, ordinals and formulas; explored bounds cannot be global certificates.\n\nRecovery repairs reject lossy rational-record coercion, malformed or unsupported domains, generated-name collisions, duplicate finite values and repeated contract identities. A bounded domain with 10^30 integer values stops after one completed cell and retains its exact unvisited cardinality. An independent integer predicate oracle checks disjoint coverage of overlapping guards. Changed principal and rate inputs, including reversed endpoint order, verify that P03 bounds come from generated inputs rather than fixed expected amounts.\n\nThe claimed target is the declared rational-linear family. The finite comparisons compute exactly the enumerated assignment sets; algebra supplies the continuous endpoint comparator. This establishes these tested invariants within the profile. It does not establish arbitrary-history completeness. Uncertainty admission checks validate records and declared permissions, not the truth of underlying evidence or professional accounting eligibility. Grouping covers unhedged additive bullet debt with no within-horizon maturity; year fractions are explicit assumptions. Probability atoms are declared disjoint economic hypotheses; their external interpretation is a modeling assumption.\n\n| Decision | Primary criterion | Veto status | Main uncertainty | Next justified action | Not concluded |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| PASS for bounded engineering checks | Independent finite sets, integration and endpoint assertions | protection=True; tests=True; missing=[]; duplicates=[] | shared solver defects, omitted templates, external admission truth | independent result review if PASS; local repair if FAIL | accounting validity, empirical forecast validity, human acceptance or closure of G1–G18 |\n\nEngineering, numerical and interpretation ledgers remain separate: implementation and executed invariants are recorded above; exact results concern only declared constraints; full-company accounting and empirical forecasts remain unevaluated. No stochastic comparison or method ranking is made.\n\nThe strongest alternative explanation is a shared modeling error between construction and fixtures. Independent posting replay, perturbed inputs and analytic endpoint checks reduce that risk. An in-profile counterexample would overturn this result. The weakest evidence is breadth: these are small deterministic cases, not arbitrary accounting histories.\n\nActual command: `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p04.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04 --execution-inventory data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P04/execution-0/pre-edit-files.json --approved-plan data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P04/approved-plan.json`. Python 3.11.15, Z3 4.16.0, CPU only with GPU devices intentionally hidden. Wall time: 4.406002 seconds. Seeds: N/A, deterministic. Git provenance is unavailable; conformance.json contains content hashes and protection comparisons for 384 files. Current approved plan: `data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P04/approved-plan.json`. Original design: `data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04/approved-plan.json`. Current execution inventory: `data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P04/execution-0/pre-edit-files.json`; historical inventory: `data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04/phase-entry-inventory.json`. Both references and their hashes are recorded separately. The manifest distinguishes all phase contributions from files changed during this execution.\n\nResiduals: nonlinear inference, continuous probability inference, unbounded integer search, template discovery, general aggregation equivalence, accounting validity, forecast validity and human acceptance remain open. All MC01–MC35/G1–G18 retain wider obligations.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
