{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '77,82p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\nsed -n '124,163p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '98,118p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\nsed -n '174,192p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\"","aggregated_output":"| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\n| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\n| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\n| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\n| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\n| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\n### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\n\nEvidence: [initial corporate scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/08-modules.tex:41)\nand [report production](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:209).\n\nSales, inventory, payroll, fixed assets and working capital are named, but\nrecognition, measurement and transition rules are not supplied as a coherent\nreference package. There is no complete company example joining accruals,\nsettlements, cost of sales, depreciation, closing, cash-flow classification\nand changes in equity. Consolidation, foreign-currency translation and\nrestatement have sound stated requirements but lack equivalent numerical\nspecifications. The tests for these operations mostly describe desired\nproperties without complete inputs and expected outputs.\n\nRequired repair: provide one deliberately bounded corporate profile with an\nopening state, event schedules, journal templates and all statement mappings.\nCarry it across annual and interim periods, including a correction and one\nperimeter or currency case. Every supported operation needs its assumptions,\npreconditions, state changes and expected reports; explicit exclusions are\nacceptable. A balanced financing illustration does not specify this package.\n\n### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\n\nEvidence: [proposed demonstrator](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:128),\n[ingestion](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:6),\nand [example request](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:234).\n\nThe document proposes a real company and a synthetic company but does not\ninstantiate either as a full disclosure package. There is no named filing\nset with source passages, extracted records, alternative readings, resolved\ncross-references, history constraints and resulting conditional statements.\nThe mathematical example starts after the consequential interpretation work\nhas already been supplied by hand.\n\nRequired repair: add a complete synthetic fixture whose hidden history is known\nand a bounded, named real annual/interim disclosure case. Show representative\nnotes including narrative qualifications, missing terms, a contradiction and\na revised comparative. A worked specification can be written before the\nengine exists; the gap is not simply the absence of production code.\n\n### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\n\nRequirements: MC14, MC18. Refines G6 and crosses modelling/execution requirements.\nEvidence: [three scenario meanings](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/03-literature.tex:149),\n[information timing](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:121),\nand [scenario grammar](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:51).\n\nThe literature chapter promises to distinguish an imposed exogenous path,\nan observational conditional forecast and an intervention. The surface example\nonly sets a driver. The record/API specification does not supply complete\nmode-specific semantics for conditioning or replacing equations. Similarly,\nbehavioural and measurement plugins are told to use permissible information,\nbut the available-information object and its access rules are unspecified.\n\nRequired evidence: declare supported scenario kinds and represent them in the\nschema. A first release can explicitly support exogenous stress only without\nclaiming the other operations. Show how a manager and an allowance calculation\nreceive current information while future simulated outcomes remain hidden.\nExplain when new observed evidence updates historical weights and why merely\nselecting a hypothetical stress does not do so.\n\n### G18. Reproducibility needs identity and replay definitions, not only fields\n\nRequirements: MC25, MC34. Refines G2, G9 and G10.\nEvidence: [three identities](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:21),\n[event replay](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:115),\nand [manifest](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/09-implementation.tex:175).\n\nThe draft requires evidence/model/execution identifiers, idempotency and stable\nrandom streams, but does not fully define canonical representation, event\nidentity, stream allocation or semantics-preserving migrations. Without these,\ndifferent implementations can assign different identities or change simulated\ndraws after a harmless branch reorder while claiming to follow the same design.\n\nRequired evidence: explicit canonicalisation and identity rules, version and\nmigration contracts, and replay examples covering formatting changes, evidence\ncorrections, reordered independent events, duplicate event IDs and branch order.\nSpecify which results must be identical and which numerical comparisons have a\njustified tolerance. No new cryptographic-attestation system is implied.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
