ssion:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:552:class AlternativeBinding:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:560:class CompileBindings:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:686:def _unique(rows, attr, key, code):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:693:def _validate_bindings(bindings: CompileBindings) -> None:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:823:def _empty_ir() -> dict[str, Any]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:838:def _diag(code: str, message: str, location: str, capability: Optional[str] = None,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:843:class _Compiler:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1528:def _numeric_type(typ: str) -> bool:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1532:def _is_scalar(typ: str) -> bool:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1536:def _merge_context(left: Optional[str], right: Optional[str], owner: str, compiler: _Compiler) -> Optional[str]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1542:def _literal_value(expr: Expr, where: str) -> Any:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1550:def _arithmetic(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Any:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1564:def _compare(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Optional[bool]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1571:def _fold_bool(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Optional[bool]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1577:def compile_program(program: Program, bindings: CompileBindings,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1598:def _load_schema() -> dict[str, Any]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1605:def _invalid(code: str, message: str, location: str) -> Diagnostic:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1609:def _nodes(ir: Mapping[str, Any]) -> tuple[dict[str, tuple[str, Mapping[str, Any]]], Optional[Diagnostic]]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1624:def _ref(nodes: Mapping[str, tuple[str, Mapping[str, Any]]], identifier: str,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1633:class _IRTypeChecker:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1770:def _expression_bounds(identifier, nodes):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1793:def validate_ir(ir: Mapping[str, Any], bindings: CompileBindings,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2076:def _validate_profile_integrity(ir, bindings, nodes, checker):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2144:class _Symbolic:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2148:def evaluate_expression(ir: Mapping[str, Any], identifier: str,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2201:def semantic_projection(ir: Mapping[str, Any] | None) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n        p.slots=1\n    except UnsupportedFragment as exc:p.unsupported.append(str(exc))\n    return p\n\n\nclass FiniteMeasure:\n    def __init__(self, atoms, justification, used=()):\n        if not justification:raise ValueError('explicit joint-measure justification required')\n        self.atoms=deepcopy(atoms);self.justification=justification;self.used=set(used)\n        ids=[a['id'] for a in atoms]\n        if len(ids)!=len(set(ids)) or not atoms:raise ValueError('distinct joint atoms required')\n        hypotheses = [a.get('hypothesis') for a in atoms]\n        if any(not isinstance(h, dict) or not h for h in hypotheses):\n            raise ValueError('explicit complete finite economic assignments required')\n        keys = set(hypotheses[0])\n        if any(set(h) != keys or any(isinstance(v, (dict,list)) for v in h.values()) for h in hypotheses):\n            raise ValueError('joint hypotheses require the same complete scalar coordinates')\n        if len({json.dumps(h,sort_keys=True) for h in hypotheses}) != len(hypotheses):\n            raise ValueError('overlapping identical economic hypotheses')\n        weights=[rational(a['weight']) for a in atoms]\n        if any(w<0 for w in weights) or sum(weights)!=1:raise ValueError('joint weights must sum to one')\n    def update(self, likelihood, information_blocks):\n        blocks=set(information_blocks)\n        if not blocks or len(blocks) != len(information_blocks) or blocks & self.used:raise ValueError('repeated/missing information block')\n        if set(likelihood)!={a['id'] for a in self.atoms}:raise ValueError('likelihood must cover every atom')\n        ls={k:rational(v) for k,v in likelihood.items()}\n        if any(v<0 or v>1 for v in ls.values()):raise ValueError('invalid event likelihood')\n        weights=[rational(a['weight'])*ls[a['id']] for a in self.atoms]; total=sum(weights)\n        if total==0:raise ValueError('zero-probability conditioning')\n        new=[dict(a,weight=str(w/total)) for a,w in zip(self.atoms,weights)]\n        return FiniteMeasure(new,self.justification,self.used|blocks)\n    def event(self, ids):\n        ids=set(ids)\n        if ids-{a['id'] for a in self.atoms}:raise ValueError('unknown atom')\n        return sum((rational(a['weight']) for a in self.atoms if a['id'] in ids),F(0))\n    def summary(self):\n        mass={};mean=F(0);available=True\n        for a in self.atoms:\n            w=rational(a['weight']); status=a['status'];mass[status]=mass.get(status,F(0))+w\n            if a.get('outcome') is None:\n                if w:available=False\n            else:mean+=w*rational(a['outcome'])\n        return {'mass':{k:str(v) for k,v in mass.items()},'mean':str(mean) if available else None,\n                'normalised_over_successful_only':False}\n\n\ndef weighted_summary(measure):\n    if not isinstance(measure,FiniteMeasure):raise ValueError('unweighted families have no mean')\n    return measure.summary()\n\\section{A correction changes what was knowable}\n\nThe original interim filing reported revenue of 120 and receivables of 30.\nTen units of revenue had been recorded before delivery. Its tax expense was\n3.5, profit 14 and equity 80. The annual filing subsequently corrected the\ninterim revenue and receivable by 10 and recognised the excess tax payment as\nprepaid tax of 2. Corrected interim profit is 6 and equity is 72, as above.\nThe original statement remains an accurate record of what was published, even\nthough its revenue recognition was wrong under the stated delivery rule.\n\nFor the temporal fixture, the original report becomes available on 1 August\n2024 and is ingested on 3 August. The correction and annual report become\navailable on 2 March 2025 and are ingested on 5 March. An investor-information\nquery as of September 2024 returns 120. The same query as of 3 March 2025\nreturns 110 when evaluated using the subsequently acquired archive. A query\nthat additionally asks what the database contained on 4 March still returns\n120. Publication and ingestion answer different questions.\n\nThe annual total 260 and corrected interim total 110 share revision group\n\\code{v2}, so second-half revenue is $260-110=150$. Subtracting the original\n120 would yield 140, but that result mixes incompatible revisions. The query\nmust reject the subtraction unless a reviewed compatibility relationship\nsupports it. A later date alone does not establish such a relationship.\nliabilities 277,327 and equity 66,758. The interim debt note's rounded\n``94.8 billion'' and the statement's 94,804 million can coexist; their\nprecision differs. Treating them as conflicting exact numbers would create\nan artificial infeasibility.\n\nTo demonstrate a source-to-forecast calculation, freeze the interim balance\nsheet and apply a \\emph{marginal} financing stress for a following 13-week\nperiod: a 200-basis-point rate increase, no principal change, no offsetting\nhedge beyond the explicitly selected exposure, immediate cash settlement and\nno tax effect. An assumed effective floating exposure $E=14{,}575$ million\nproduces $0.02\\times(13/52)E=72.875$ million additional interest. This exposure\nuses the annual notional as a conditional input; it is not asserted to be the\ninterim net sensitivity. Under that condition, debit interest expense and\ncredit cash by 72.875. The resulting marginal statements have cash 30,226.125,\nassets 344,012.125, liabilities 277,327, equity 66,685.125, profit and comprehensive\nincome of $-72.875$, and operating cash flow of $-72.875$ relative to the frozen\nbaseline. The balance-sheet difference equals the equity difference exactly.\n\nIf exposure is instead only restricted to $0\\leq E\\leq14{,}575$, the\nconditional added interest lies in $[0,72.875]$ before monetary rounding. That\nrestriction is a stress assumption and is not claimed to bound every real\nApple exposure. This real case verifies evidence, context, mappings and a\ncoherent marginal propagation. Northstar supplies the complete-company\nforecast; a complete Apple forecast remains dependent on its unmodelled\noperations and undisclosed terms.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
